# Pack Your Bag - Monorepo Standards

Turborepo monorepo using Yarn 4 (Berry).

# Communication

- Be succinct and to the point in all your code, documentation and explainations unless explicitly asked for more details. Avoid fluff.
- Pattern: [thing] [action] [reason]. [next step].

## Architecture Anchors

- `apps/*` contains deployable apps/services.
- `packages/*` contains shared libraries and configs.
- Prefer shared configs: `@repo/typescript-config`, `@repo/eslint-config`, `@repo/vitest-config`.

## Execution Rules

- Use `yarn`. Never use `npm` or `pnpm`.
- Use `turbo run <task>` for workspace-wide tasks.
- Do not add/remove dependencies. Tell me the changes you need.
- Respect TypeScript/ESLint strictness. Never use `any`.

## Safety Guardrails

- DO NOT modify `docker-compose.yml`, `.devcontainer/`, or any file in the root directory unless specifically asked.
- DO NOT attempt to create or migrate databases automatically.
- DO NOT install new global packages.
- If a task requires changing infrastructure, STOP and ask for confirmation first.
